TargetCheck test-only instrumentation: named parse_content_range cases

Status: local TargetCheck addition for the Wget example. It is not an
upstream GNU Wget change. It is applied first, identically, to every
variant (unpatched, first-fix and complete), before any fix.

It changes only the TESTING build used by the tests/unit-tests program.
The wget program and its feature set are unchanged.

  tests/content-range-cases.c (new): named cases that call the
      production, file-static parse_content_range(), following the
      upstream MinUnit convention (a test returns NULL or a failure
      message), with named assertion diagnostics.
  src/http.c: include that file inside the existing TESTING section, so
      the cases share the production translation unit.
  tests/unit-tests.c, tests/unit-tests.h: with command-line arguments,
      run only the named cases, flushing stdout before each case;
      without arguments, the upstream test list runs unchanged.

